  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed rear extension, by reason of its excessive depth, would fail to be subservient to the host historic building and would result in an incongruous addition that disrupts the established 3m rear building line prevalent along this terrace. Consequently, the proposal would result in less than substantial harm to the Grade II listed building by&amp;nbsp;failing to conserve and enhance the significance of the listed building and failing to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the conservation area.&amp;nbsp;This harm is not outweighed by any public benefits, rendering the proposal contrary to Sections 16 and 66 of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990; Section 16 of the National Planning Policy Framework; policies D3 (Optimising site layout through the design-led approach), D4 (Delivering good design) and HC1 (&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-bd0ee21e-7fff-273d-76df-a065c0e13962&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;&quot;&gt;Heritage conservation and growth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;) of the London Plan (2021), and policies LP1 (&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;&quot;&gt;Design Quality and Local Character&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;and LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets) of the Hackney Local Plan LP33 (2020) and the Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2025).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;"
  ],
